  "grafo_evidencia": {
    "nodes": [
      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "93bb7df7-8a25-5a78-858f-545ed571f7b0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Concepts: plant taxonomy, genus reclassification\n- Plants/Genera: Rhodochiton, Platystemon, Lophospermum, Asarina, Maurandya, Holmgrenanthe, Mabrya, Neogaerrhinum\n- Families: Plantaginaceae, poppy family\n- Places: southern Mexico, Guatemala, North America\n\nFacts:\n- Rhodochiton is a genus of flowering plants in the family Plantaginaceae that is native to southern Mexico and neighboring Guatemala.\n- Platystemon is a monotypic genus of flowering plants in the poppy family that contains the single species Platystemon californicus, commonly called creamcups.\n- Lophospermum has a close relationship with other genera, especially Maurandya and Rhodochiton, and this relationship has caused confusion over the names of some species.\n- Species from North America that were formerly placed in Asarina are now placed in Holmgrenanthe, Lophospermum, Mabrya, Maurandya, and Neogaerrhinum.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "148be4b1-2efc-5f4f-afcc-af2ae12d7f30",
        "text": "Page: Rhodochiton. Sentence: Rhodochiton is a genus of flowering plants within the family Plantaginaceae, native to southern Mexico and neighbouring Guatemala.\nPage: Platystemon. Sentence: Platystemon is a monotypic genus of flowering plants in the poppy family containing the single species Platystemon californicus, which is known by the common name creamcups.\nPage: Lophospermum. Sentence: The close relationship with some other genera, particularly \"Maurandya\" and \"Rhodochiton\", has led to confusion over the names of some species.\nPage: Asarina. Sentence: Species from North America formerly placed in the genus \"Asarina\" are now placed in \"Holmgrenanthe\", \"Lophospermum\", \"Mabrya\" and \"Maurandya\", as well as \"Neogaerrhinum\".",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
